<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="6f84840c-24c9-5a2f-838c-22f53fdac5de" activityNameId="fe98b07b-9e91-5e79-9464-093a6f25aae2" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, uranium tailings, non-radioactive emissions</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, uranium tailings, non-radioactive emissions
na;
Synonyms: uranium tails; 
UUID: bc6967a3-2916-4fbc-a3f5-2b0e5029ee93
Waste-specific emissions for uranium tailings impoundment leachate. Mixture of a generic dry site (53%) and generic wet site (47%). Short- and long-term emissions to air from dry site (wind erosion of evaporites). Short- and long-term emissions to groundwater from wet site (infiltration leaching).; Geography: Data refers to a worldwide average. Dataset contains the mixture of two different generic sites: 53% dry site (actual evaporation &gt; precipitation) and 47% wet site  (actual evaporation &lt; precipitation), according to the worldwide uranium tailings production in 2006.
Location:  Data refers to a worldwide average. Dataset contains the mixture of two different generic sites: 53% dry site (actual evaporation &gt; precipitation) and 47% wet site  (actual evaporation &lt; precipitation), according to the worldwide uranium tailings production in 2006.
Technology: Mechanically stable tailings impoundment. Closure with clay barrier and reduction of leachate flow for the initial 2000 years. Uranium production from in-situ leaching (ISL) is not heedded.
Time period: Average uranium tailings composition from literature references. Transfer coefficients from prospective model, specific to uranium tailings.
Production volume: 21.46 Mio t/a tailings generation (11.54 in dry sites / 9.919 in wet sites)
Sampling: Tailings model based on observed leachate concentrations in literature. Extrapolated to 80'000 years heeding chemical characteristics. Initial tailings composition from various literature sources.  
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: Uncertainty of waste input composition data derived from large literature survey. Mean long-term emissions are the emissions during a generic ecological planning horizon (80'000a). Maximal (upper boundary) long-term emissions are the complete emissions of all landfilled material.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_bc6967a3-2916-4fbc-a3f5-2b0e5029ee93.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
